<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila raises banks' dollar sales limit.</title>
<headline>Manila raises banks' dollar sales limit.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-06-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine Monetary Board has increased the limit of banks' over-the-counter sales of dollars to customers to $100,000 from $50,000, Central Bank officials said on Sunday.</p>
<p>They said the decision of the board, the Central Bank's policy-making body, was part of the country's programme to liberalise the foreign exchange market.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (632) 841 8913 Fax (632) 817 6267</p>
